# OFF COURSE

You are working for _off__course.

Off Course is an independent creative studio.

We build websites, murals, identities and digital experiences for artists,
cafes, bookshops, cultural organisations and independent businesses.

We are not a software agency.

We are not a marketing agency.

We are not a startup studio.

We are closer to an independent design magazine.

Everything we create should feel thoughtful, calm and contemporary.

Canonical design system: `docs/design-system.md`  
Canonical IA: `docs/information-architecture.md`

---

## Philosophy

Good work deserves to be found.

Technology exists to support stories.

Design should never feel generic.

Every project should have its own world.

---

## Two worlds

```
A project never needs to become both worlds.
GET LOST can exist independently.
GET FOUND can exist independently.
Only bridge them when it creates meaningful value.
```

### GET LOST — Expression · Ideas become physical

Murals · Illustration · Brand Identity · Installations · Creative Direction · Experimental Visual

Case behaviour: place, scale, texture, paint, process, imperfect crops — never open on device mockups.

### GET FOUND — Discovery · Ideas become accessible

Websites · Systems · Applications · CMS · Automation · AI · Internal Tools

Case behaviour: clarity, structure, access — artwork/story before screens when the work is cultural.

### Bridge is metadata, not navigation

Never a third nav category. Never a Bridge archive page.

---

## Quiet navigation (locked)

Permanent header only:

- Brand → Index
- About
- Archive
- Contact
- Grid → editorial full-screen menu

Do NOT put GET LOST / GET FOUND in the permanent header.

Worlds are discovered via homepage radio + editorial body.
Menu may list them as secondary destinations (not chrome).

---

## Design principles

Editorial before interface.

Typography before decoration.

Whitespace before components.

One purpose per viewport.

Journey words (signal, frequency, coordinates, route, arrival, mileage…)
are sparse metadata — never a game HUD.

---

## Never generate / never restore

- SaaS UI · glassmorphism · neon · crypto · startup landings
- Large floating pill navigation
- All-black rounded card walls (ZeroFrame / zf-* patterns)
- Framer CardStack / 3D carousel portfolio toys as the Found system
- Walala marquee tile grids as the Lost system
- Duplicate navigation systems
- Invented awards, metrics, clients, locations, or outcomes

If a previous experiment (`FoundPillNav`, `FoundWorksIndex`, `zf-*`,
`ProjectTile`, card-stack stages) appears in git history, do not revive it.

Active system components:

- `SiteHeader` / `SiteMenu`
- `HomeCanvas` / `HomeEditorial`
- `LostIndex` / `LostCaseStudy`
- `FoundIndex` / `FoundCaseStudy`
- `ArchiveIndex`

---

## Always ask

Why does this project exist?

What emotion should visitors remember?

How can interaction support the story?

Only after answering these questions should implementation begin.

---

## Code philosophy

Keep components modular.

Accessibility first.

Performance is part of the design.

Animations communicate meaning — no bounce / elastic.

Prefer maintainable solutions over impressive solutions.
